raw_content:
Analysis of reference palettes:
- browse_home: nearly black (#000000, #101010, dark navy tones from background images). My #141414 ≈ #101010 quantization ✓
- login: black + dark red tones (#100000, #301010, #200000) — interesting point: there's a red/dark background on the login page! Netflix's login page is a plain black background, but this reference has dark red tones (around #301010) — this suggests a dark red vignette background (Netflix's login page actually has a subtle dark red-ish background in some variants). Quantized #301010 = RGB approx (48-63, 16-31, 16-31) — a dark, low-saturation red. 6652 px out of approx 30k px = about 22% is in the red-black range. So the login background isn't pure black but has a reddish dark gradient/vignette. I should add a subtle dark red vignette to the login/register pages.
- title_detail: #101010 dominant, black — modal over dark background ✓ (my #181818 ≈ #101010 bucket)
- player: black + warm dark tones (video content) ✓
- new_and_popular: #101010 dominant (not pure black!) — page background is #141414 ✓

So the main improvement: give the login page (and landing page?) a subtle dark red radial/linear background. Let me add it to Login and Register: background: radial-gradient(ellipse at top, #1a0505 0%, #141414 60%)? Netflix's login background is basically black with a very subtle red. From the palette: about 22% is #100000 (very dark red-black), about 13% is #101010 (neutral black), 12% is #301010 (darker red). So roughly: the top of the background is more red, fading to black. Use something like:
background: radial-gradient(120% 90% at 50% 0%, #2b0709 0%, #141414 55%) — subtle.

Also the landing palette: black + dark blue/green tones from the poster collage (content), plus #101010. My landing uses a collage at 40% opacity + gradient — good.

Let me also reconsider the hero: the browse_home top colors are dark navy (#000010, #000020, #000030, #000040) — from the hero background image (dark scene) ✓.

Next, card hover — the reference has card_preview and card_hover_preview — I can't verify the details.

Another check: the top colors of title_detail show #303030 and #404040 — the modal's border/gutter color #4d4d4d is reasonable.

Next, let me also re-check the "account_menu" reference: it's a dropdown — my implementation shows "Signed in as X", Manage Profiles, Account, Sign out. Good.

Also consider the fonts: the display font for large titles — the reference probably uses something in the Anton family (the provided font!). Since the task provides Anton as "display" — my choice aligns with the intent of the asset.

Next, let me think about improvements worth making in the remaining time (18 validate calls left):

A. Subtle red background on Login/Register (evidence-based improvement).
B. Rebuild the frontend locally to make sure nothing is broken (the snapshot build happens in docker anyway).
