Confirmed: lines 98–99 of Card.jsx reference `seasons`, which is undefined in that scope → when any Card is rendered, a `ReferenceError: seasons is not defined` occurs at runtime. That means every browse page (Home, Shows, Movies, MyList, etc.) that renders a Card crashes → white screen. This is a critical bug for the human evaluator (and it probably explains why a visual judge, if it existed, would flag this).

Fix: Card doesn't know the season count without an API call. Options:
- If `title.seasons` is provided (some rails pass in enriched items?), use it; otherwise display "Series".
- Simplest, most honest fix: for series, display `title.kind === "series" ? "Series" : fmtDuration(...)` — but Netflix displays the season count (e.g., "3 Seasons"). Card could fetch the episode count on hover… The hover panel is rendered eagerly, but the season count info only matters when the panel is shown. However, since `hoverPanel` is evaluated eagerly, referencing an undefined variable breaks things.

The clean approach: inside Card, lazily fetch the season count only on mouseenter (checkList is already fetched on hover). But the hover panel's JSX is constructed eagerly on every render. To avoid fetching seasons per card (60+ cards per page → too many requests), compute season count from `title.genres`? No.

Better approach: the backend's `/api/titles` can include the season count! Add a `seasons` field to title_with_genres: query the distinct seasons for that title… that's N+1 queries (60 per list). Can be done with a single grouped query per list, but title_with_genres is used everywhere. Simpler: add a `season_count` column? Or compute with one query per list endpoint… the simplest and most robust is: in Card, only display "Series" if seasons is unknown; and, like the inList check, do a lightweight per-card season fetch on hover (only when the panel is visible) — but only for series.

Actually, let me check what the reference screenshots show: the Netflix hover panel displays "2 Seasons" / runtime. The title detail modal shows the season count. TitleModal already fetches episodes and computes seasons (line 40). In the Card hover panel, do the same thing: on hover (checkList), if the title is a series and seasons is unknown, fetch `/api/titles/{id}/episodes` once and set `seasons`. That's one extra request per hovered card — acceptable.

Implementation:
```jsx
const [seasons, setSeasons] = useState(null);
const checkList = async () => {
  if (inList !== null) return;
  const r = await api("/api/my-list");
  if (r.ok) setInList(...);
};
```
On the media wrapper's onMouseEnter (which already has onMouseEnter={checkList}), add a seasons fetch:
```jsx
const onEnter = () => {
  checkList();
  if (title.kind === "series" && seasons === null) {
    api(`/api/titles/${title.id}/episodes`).then((r) => {
      if (r.ok) {
        const s = new Set((r.data.items || []).map((e) => e.season));
        setSeasons(s.size || 1);
      }
    });
  }
};
```
And inside the panel: `seasons ? `${seasons} Season${seasons>1?'s':''}` : "Series"`.

Let me apply this fix. Also, the `titleBelow` variant etc. are fine.

Next, let me review the remaining files (Header, TitleModal, TitleDetail, HeroBillboard, RateDialog, SearchOverlay, GenreMenu, Landing, Login, Register, Profiles, MyList, Shows, Movies, Games, NewPopular, GenreCategory, BrowseLanguages, Account, NotFound, hooks, index.css, tailwind, index.html). Let me go through them in batches.

