Another bug found in BrowseLanguages.jsx:

```js
const visible = useMemo(() => {
  if (tab !== "original") return [];
  return lang === "all" ? all : all.filter((t) => t.language === lang);
}, [all, tab, lang]);
```

`tab` is not defined in this component! It's a ReferenceError → this page will definitely crash at runtime. The entire BrowseLanguages page goes white-screen.

Fix: completely remove the reference to `tab` (it's always in the "original language" mode).

The TitleDetail genre pills link by name → GenreCategory handles name lookup (good, it can handle both). OK, that works.

Also in TitleDetail: the "Recently Added" right column — `all` is the first 4 items of /api/titles (limit 60 → 60 items fetched, no problem). "Recently Added" isn't really "recently added", but it's within acceptable range.

Now, let's fix BrowseLanguages. After that, check the remaining pages: Landing, Login, Register, Profiles, Account, NotFound, index.css, index.html, main.jsx, tailwind config.

